# HowManyTaxes agent rule

Before changing tax math, budgets, spending data, or methodology UI copy, read and follow:

`docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md`

## Product north star

Help users see how **their** federal tax dollars map to real government programs, using **official** spending/revenue sources — not hardcoded guesses.

## Hard constraints

- Separate **income tax** (general fund) from **payroll/SE taxes** (Social Security / Medicare HI). Do not allocate Social Security primarily as a slice of income tax.
- Prefer Treasury Fiscal Data (MTS), OMB Historical Tables, IRS, and SSA over secondary blogs.
- Every budget figure needs `fiscalYear`, source URL, and retrieval/cache metadata.
- Handle employee vs self-employed FICA/SECA (wage base, 92.35% SE base, deductible half of SE tax).
- Keep estimators honest: list omissions (credits, AMT, itemizing, etc.) in the UI.

## Implementation preferences

- Pure, testable calc modules; thin React pages.
- Version tax parameters by tax year (`2025`, `2026`, …).
- Cache government API responses; do not call uncached Treasury on every request.
- Prefer MTS/OMB budget **functions** over ad-hoc political line items.

When the brief and code disagree, update the brief or fix the code so they match — do not silently diverge.
